{"file":"wai-suite-0.4.0-v2.zip","bytes":725356,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"wai-suite","description":"Sustainable software product development with Claude Code: 13 skills for the engineering lifecycle — plan, build, test, review, audit — built to keep architecture maintainable and clean and security first-class while agents write the code. The working premise, drawn from field runs: even frontier models lose context, are confident when wrong, and forget rules — so nothing here relies on the model remembering; each goal gets a gate, a rule, or a deterministic check, and whether a PR may merge is decided by a script with an exit code and, above it, a human. Ships the merge gate, the quality-catalog system (one master, three generated variants), 29 enforcement scripts and 497 cases, founded on bugs that shipped and grown into regression guards.","version":"0.4.0","license":"MIT","repository":"https://github.com/woldinius/wai-skill-suite","homepage":"https://github.com/woldinius/wai-skill-suite","keywords":["lifecycle","software-engineering","sustainable-development","clean-architecture","maintainability","security","merge-gate","quality-gate","code-review","quality-catalog","testing","security-audit","architecture-audit"]}],"skills":[{"path":".claude/skills/wai-architecture-audit/SKILL.md","name":"wai-architecture-audit","description":"Periodic, whole-codebase structural-health audit: architectural drift, coupling, god-services, dead code — and the subtle part, semantic redundancy, inconsistency and cross-surface dead-ends — measured as a trend against a persisted architecture baseline. Use it to check the whole app, not one change: \"audit the codebase\", \"is it decoupled/modular\", \"find drift/dead code/redundancy\", \"did we accumulate tech debt\", \"run the periodic audit\". Not for the security sweep (wai-security-audit), a single PR (wai-pr-review), a fix (wai-implementation) or setup (wai-init).","headings":["Architecture & Structural-Health Audit","Platform context","Stance","Process","Severity & trend","Output format","Architecture & Structural-Health Audit: [repo] · [YYYY-MM-DD]","Metrics snapshot","Findings","Semantic redundancy, inconsistency & dead-ends (proposals — behavioral risk, not auto-applied)","Dead code & safe cleanups (apply on approval)","Architecture baseline, design-principle & catalog proposals","Positives — what's holding up well","▶ Recommended next (ranked actions)","References","Git & PR","Related Skills"],"name_hint":"wai · architecture · 审查","description_zh":"定期审计整个代码库结构健康，检查架构漂移、耦合、巨型服务、死代码及语义冗余、不一致和跨界面死路，对照持久架构基线衡量趋势；不用于安全扫描、单PR、修复或初始化。"},{"path":".claude/skills/wai-cicd/SKILL.md","name":"wai-cicd","description":"One-time setup of GitHub-native CI/CD for a backend+web repo (Actions, GHCR, Docker Compose over SSH to your own Linux server, any provider) — and owner of the merge gate that makes \"green checks\" trustworthy. Creates Dockerfiles, compose, a Caddy proxy, the Actions required-check gate, the branch-protection ruleset, CODEOWNERS, PR template, deploy script and runbook. GitHub-only by design; mobile store delivery is wai-mobile-release. Use it for: \"set up CI/CD\", \"deploy to my server\", \"create GitHub Actions\", \"containerize\", \"wire required checks\". Not for implementation, tests, PR review or the catalog (wai-init).","headings":["CI/CD & Deployment Setup","What this skill produces","Stance","Process","Scan checklist","The deploy model","Merge gate & branch protection","Relation to the quality catalog","Output format — setup report","CI/CD setup: [repo name]","Created / Changed","Secrets (to be stored — no values in the repo)","Manual server steps","To verify / Follow-up tasks","Principles","Related Skills"],"name_hint":"wai · cicd","description_zh":"为后端与Web仓库一次性配置GitHub原生CI/CD，通过Actions、GHCR和SSH Docker Compose部署自有Linux，建立Dockerfiles、Caddy、必需检查、分支保护、CODEOWNERS、PR模板及运行手册；移动商店交付另用mobile-release。"},{"path":".claude/skills/wai-implementation/SKILL.md","name":"wai-implementation","description":"Default skill for implementing changes — the senior fullstack doer. Plans first (risk and blast radius), builds on the requirement''s `agent/**` branch, self-reviews, and opens the PR. Invoked for any implementation, bug fix or code change — or a described behavior that needs one: \"implement X\", \"fix\", \"bug\", \"returns error 503\", \"build\", \"change\", \"adjust\", \"refactor\", \"X should do Y\". Not for reviewing a finished PR (wai-pr-review) or extensive greenfield planning (wai-requirements-planning).","headings":["Implementation","Platform context","Stance","Process","Affected surfaces & concerns","Output format — plan","Implementation plan: [short description]","Solution approach","Improvement / Alternative","Risk · Ambiguity · Blast radius","Process","Test needs (e2e, later)","Tests","Git & PR","Principles","Related Skills"],"name_hint":"wai · implementation","description_zh":"先评估风险和影响范围，再在需求agent分支实现修改、修复或重构，自审并开PR；不负责已完成PR评审或大型新项目规划。"},{"path":".claude/skills/wai-init/SKILL.md","name":"wai-init","description":"Bootstrap and re-runnable updater for the wAI suite: deep-scans a repo, then writes its surface-scoped quality catalog (`docs/architecture/quality-attributes.md`) and testing strategy, sized to the project. Asks the setup questions — solo or team, protect `main`, docs language, catalog tier, learning mode — BEFORE writing what they configure, and keeps existing docs unless you ask for a reset. Use it to set the suite up, or to reconcile it later: \"set up the skills\", \"initialize the project\", \"onboard this repo\", \"create/update the quality catalog\", \"bootstrap\", \"tune the skills\". Not for planning, implementation or PR review — it only lays the foundation.","headings":["Init (bootstrap & update)","What this skill produces","Stance","Sizing — the catalog is the suite's token budget","Process","Scan checklist","Tailoring rules","Output format — setup report","Principles","Related Skills"],"name_hint":"wai · init","description_zh":"初始化或重复更新wAI套件，深入扫描仓库后生成按界面范围的质量属性目录和测试策略；先询问团队、main保护、文档语言、目录层级及学习模式，保留既有文档，除非要求重置。"},{"path":".claude/skills/wai-learning-gap/SKILL.md","name":"wai-learning-gap","description":"Personal learning mode (cloze coding + Leitner), tech-stack agnostic — opt-in per developer, never repo-wide. Active ONLY for a human who has a personal ledger under `~/.claude/learning/`; with no ledger it does nothing and creates nothing, so colleagues stay untouched. It plants exactly one learning gap (🧩 LEARN marker) at the end of an implementation phase, reviews the human''s solution, and moves topics through Leitner boxes. Triggers: \"learning gap\", \"hint\", \"solution\", \"learning status\", \"solved\", \"check my solution\", \"skip the gap\", \"learning mode on/off\", \"learning axes\", \"combine the building blocks\", \"learn architecture/domain\".","headings":["Learning mode: cloze coding with Leitner","Learning mode is personal, not project-wide","Ledger location (personal, outside git)","The identity lives in the ledger, not only in the path","Opt-in / opt-out (by the human)","Optional CLAUDE.md anchor (neutral, activates nobody)","Learning mode (per developer, opt-in)","Ground rules (always)","Learning axes — which KIND of line, and how each fails visibly","Flow A — plant a gap (end of every implementation phase)","Flow B — review (the human reports a solution, or the marker is gone next turn)","Flow C — expiry (gap in the way, or older than one phase)","Flow D — post-autopilot offer (opt-in, one gap, off a merged commit)","Hint escalation","Leitner due-dates","Template: marker (use each file's comment syntax)","Templates: ledger and pre-commit hook"],"name_hint":"wai · 学习 · gap","description_zh":"面向选择加入且有个人学习账本的开发者，采用填空编码及Leitner学习；在实现末尾留一个学习空缺、检查答案并推进主题，不为无账本用户或整个仓库自动建立学习状态。"},{"path":".claude/skills/wai-mobile-release/SKILL.md","name":"wai-mobile-release","description":"One-time setup of build, code signing and store delivery for a native iOS or Android repo (TestFlight/App Store Connect, or Play Console tracks) — and owner of the mobile merge gate. Creates Fastlane lanes or the Gradle release config, signing, the Actions required-check gate, branch-protection ruleset, CODEOWNERS, PR template and release runbook. Use it for: \"set up the iOS build\", \"Fastlane\", \"TestFlight\", \"code signing\", \"Play Console\", \"mobile CI\", \"staged rollout\". Not for the backend+web pipeline (wai-cicd), implementation, tests or PR review.","headings":["Mobile Release Setup","Platform context","What this skill produces","Stance","Process","Merge gate & store submission","Relation to the quality catalog","Output format — setup report","Mobile release setup: [repo name]","Created / Changed","Secrets (to be stored — no values in the repo)","Manual store-console steps","To verify / Follow-up tasks","Principles","Related Skills"],"name_hint":"wai · mobile · release","description_zh":"一次性配置原生iOS/Android构建、签名及TestFlight/App Store或Play渠道交付，创建Fastlane或Gradle、Actions门禁、分支保护、CODEOWNERS、PR模板和发布手册；不负责后端Web流水线。"},{"path":".claude/skills/wai-pr-review/SKILL.md","name":"wai-pr-review","description":"Senior architecture/DevOps review of a pull request or diff against the quality catalog and the originating spec, ordered by severity — and owner of the gated auto-merge. A review lens may be named at invocation (\"review this adversarially\", \"null-hypothesis\", \"breadth\"); otherwise it follows from the change type. Use it to evaluate any PR/diff before merge: \"review this PR\", \"can this be merged\", \"check this diff\", \"code review\", \"does this fit architecturally\". Not for implementing a change (wai-implementation) or planning one (wai-requirements-planning).","headings":["PR Review","Platform context","Process","Review lens","Merge-queue mode (serial integration)","Severity levels","Output format","PR Review: [Short description of the change]","Blocker","Major","Minor","Nits","Positives","Open questions","▶ Recommended next","Principles","Related Skills"],"name_hint":"wai · pr · 评审","description_zh":"按质量目录和来源规范对PR或diff做按严重性排序的架构DevOps评审，可指定对抗、零假设或广度视角，协调门禁自动合并；不负责实现或需求规划。"},{"path":".claude/skills/wai-requirements-planning/SKILL.md","name":"wai-requirements-planning","description":"Plans and shapes a new requirement before implementation — architecture, DevOps and the cross-cutting concerns (cost, GDPR, API compatibility, resilience, token economy) surfaced early, with a \"grill me\" interview mode and alternatives when the ask is imprecise. Takes a GitHub issue at invocation (\"plan #42\"), a set of issues that form ONE requirement (\"#42 #43 #44\"), or a plain description — plus directives like \"grill me\", \"backend only\", \"no ADR\". Use it to prepare any new feature, requirement or idea: \"plan this requirement\", \"how should we build X\", \"concept for\", \"break this down into tasks\", \"do we need an ADR\". Not for an already-clarified task (wai-implementation), a finished PR (wai-pr-review), or a backlog of INDEPENDENT issues (wai-team).","headings":["Requirements Planning","Platform context","What you can be given","Process","Delta-update mode (invoked mid-implementation)","Git & PR","Output format — planning document","Requirement: [Title]","Goal & context","Scope","Architecture approach","Testing decisions (seams)","Task decomposition","Cross-cutting requirements","Architecture decisions (ADR, if relevant)","Risks & open questions","Definition of Done","▶ Recommended next"],"name_hint":"wai · requirements · 规划","description_zh":"实施前规划一个新需求，及早梳理架构DevOps、成本、GDPR、API兼容、韧性和令牌成本，可采访澄清或给替代方案，输入单issue、同一需求多issue或文字，形成任务及ADR判断。"},{"path":".claude/skills/wai-retro/SKILL.md","name":"wai-retro","description":"Periodic retrospective of the suite''s own work, built from artifacts at a threshold — never from recall. Reads the gate ledger''s report extract, the run log and git history; writes a dated, narrated report where every rate carries its raw row counts, and finishes by advancing the ledger''s report marker so the cadence resets. The collaboration level is gated until a question trace exists, and publication to the suite repo happens only on explicit request, sanitized and pseudonymized. Use it when doctor reports the verdict threshold since the last report marker, or on request: \"run the retro\", \"retrospective\", \"what did the suite do this month\", \"cut a report\", \"how many runs\". Not the per-PR review (wai-pr-review), not the structural or security audits (wai-architecture-audit / wai-security-audit), and not a metric dashboard — artifacts in, narrative out, the judgment column stays human.","headings":["Retro (periodic, artifact-derived)","Trigger","The three-layer split (ADR-0002)","Inputs — and the one document this skill does not read","Process","Report format","Suite retrospective: [repo] · [YYYY-MM-DD]","The numbers (script-derived, pasted verbatim)","What held","What broke","Calibration","Compliance — did the work leave a trace","Collaboration","Outcomes (the human's column)","▶ Recommended next","Principles","Git & PR","Related Skills"],"name_hint":"wai · retro","description_zh":"根据门禁账本、运行日志和git历史定期复盘套件工作，生成日期叙述报告，各比率带原始行数并推进报告标记；协作评价需问题轨迹，发布仅明确请求后脱敏，最终判断留给人工。"},{"path":".claude/skills/wai-security-audit/SKILL.md","name":"wai-security-audit","description":"Periodic, whole-codebase security audit — an adversarial \"how would an attacker break this\" sweep: authN/authZ and IDOR, secrets, injection (incl. prompt), SSRF, rate limiting, session/token lifecycle, dependency CVEs, crypto/TLS, tenant isolation, token-economy fraud, PII exposure. Report-only and redacted. Chains findings into ranked end-to-end attack paths. Use it to assess posture as a whole: \"security audit\", \"pentest\", \"threat model\", \"check the attack surface\", \"are we secure\", \"find vulnerabilities\". Run periodically and before a release. Not for structural health (wai-architecture-audit), a single diff (wai-pr-review) or a fix (wai-implementation).","headings":["Security Audit (adversarial, whole-codebase)","Platform context","Stance","Process","Severity & trend (security-framed)","Output format","Security Audit: [repo] · [YYYY-MM-DD]","Attack-surface snapshot","Tooling snapshot","Findings","Attack paths (kill-chains)","Defense-in-depth (hardening, lower urgency)","Security catalog proposals","Positives — what's holding up","▶ Recommended next (ranked actions)","References","Git & PR","Related Skills"],"name_hint":"wai · 安全 · 审查","description_zh":"定期或发布前对全仓安全做对抗式审计，检查认证授权、IDOR、秘密注入SSRF、限流会话、CVE、加密TLS、租户、令牌滥用及个人信息，把发现串成排序攻击路径；仅报告且脱敏。"},{"path":".claude/skills/wai-team/SKILL.md","name":"wai-team","description":"Mandated lifecycle orchestrator: works ONE or MORE GitHub issues through the full lifecycle — per issue one run of plan → implement → test → review on its own `agent/**` branch and PR, integrated serially through the merge queue, with no human gap between the phases. Requires an explicit mandate (which issues, and how decision points are handled) and hands back one collected decision list. Invoked without a named issue set, it scans the backlog and proposes — it proposes, the human mandates. Because the run is UNATTENDED, every review runs on fresh context and the merge policy is confirmed at kickoff (default: the repo''s own — solo merges each clean PR under the gate). Use it whenever issues are commissioned rather than driven phase by phase: \"run the cycle on #42\", \"work the backlog\", \"process issues #12–#18\", \"burn down the tier\", \"wai-team\". Not for a change with no issue behind it (wai-implementation) or a finished PR (wai-pr-review).","headings":["Team (lifecycle orchestrator)","Mandate first — no mandate, no team run","Process","Attended or unattended — what changes when nobody watches","Autonomous integration (opt-in, bounded)","Failure handling","Output format — team report","Team run: [issue set · date]","Held for your answer   (merge policy (b) only — the one question)","Autonomously merged   (autonomous mode only — from autonomous-merge-report.sh)","Merged","Verified — nothing to fix","▶ Your decision list","Withheld from autonomy — held for you","Blocked — waiting on a blocker that has not merged (team mode, or merge policy (b)/(c))","Skipped — claimed by someone else","Parked / failed","Cross-issue notes (since start)"],"name_hint":"wai · team","description_zh":"经明确指定issue及决策政策后，逐项在独立agent分支和PR运行规划、实现、测试、全新上下文评审，再串行合并队列，汇总决策清单；未指定时只扫描建议，启动时确认合并政策。"},{"path":".claude/skills/wai-testing/SKILL.md","name":"wai-testing","description":"Writes deterministic tests and owns the testing strategy. Mandatory targets are security, billing, GDPR and idempotency; tests never call a real model or real billing. Runs after wai-implementation on the same branch, so the PR ships with its tests. Use it to write tests, raise coverage, or set the strategy: \"write tests for X\", \"add coverage\", \"is this covered\", \"cover the billing path\", \"mock the AI models\", \"make these deterministic\". Not for implementing the feature (wai-implementation) or wiring the CI gate (wai-cicd).","headings":["Testing","Platform context","Stance","Process","Mandatory test targets (never skipped)","Testing strategy doc (default if missing)","Git & PR","Output format","Tests: [short description of the change/area]","Gate impact","▶ Recommended next","Principles","Related Skills"],"name_hint":"wai · testing","description_zh":"编写确定性测试并制定策略，重点覆盖安全、计费、GDPR及幂等，不调用真实模型或真实计费，在实现同分支为PR附测试；不负责功能实现或CI门禁。"},{"path":".claude/skills/wai/SKILL.md","name":"wai","description":"Front door and router for the wAI skill suite. Use it to orchestrate — when you are unsure which skill to start with, want a lifecycle overview, or a recommendation on what to run next: \"which skill do I use\", \"where do I start\", \"what''s next\", \"give me an overview\", \"help me orchestrate\". It only recommends the right skill and shows the hand-offs; it does not plan, implement or review itself — the human stays the orchestrator.","headings":["wai (suite router)","Operating model","The lifecycle map","How to route","Decision guide","Output format","Where you are","▶ Start with","Then, typically","Principles","Related Skills"],"name_hint":"wai","description_zh":"作为wAI套件入口推荐起始或下一技能，说明生命周期及交接；只路由建议，不自行规划、实现或评审，人工仍统筹。"}],"commands":[],"readmes":[{"path":"README.md","headings":["wai-skill-suite","Skills","Personal skills","What is different here","Why it exists — one incident","In the field — what 259 verdicts measured","What is deterministic here — and what is not"]},{"path":"docs/adr/README.md","headings":["Architecture Decision Records","The form","The records"]},{"path":"docs/learnings/README.md","headings":["Learnings — the evidence base","Where a document goes","Naming","Field reports: verbatim, foreign, and never edited","Append-only","The lifecycle","Two things that needed a decision — both decided at publication","Index"]},{"path":"docs/rationale/README.md","headings":["Rationale — why the deciding scripts are written the way they are","Why the split exists","What stays in the script, and what moves here","These files are dated evidence, not live claims"]},{"path":"docs/publication/README.md","headings":["Publication — drafts","Before anything is posted"]}],"mcp_servers":[],"config_names":[],"paths":[".claude-plugin/marketplace.json",".claude-plugin/plugin.json",".claude/skills/wai-architecture-audit/SKILL.md",".claude/skills/wai-architecture-audit/references/audit-playbook.md",".claude/skills/wai-cicd/SKILL.md",".claude/skills/wai-cicd/references/deployment-guide.md",".claude/skills/wai-cicd/references/templates/CODEOWNERS",".claude/skills/wai-cicd/references/templates/Caddyfile",".claude/skills/wai-cicd/references/templates/ci.yml",".claude/skills/wai-cicd/references/templates/deploy-ssh.yml",".claude/skills/wai-cicd/references/templates/deploy.sh",".claude/skills/wai-cicd/references/templates/docker-compose.prod.yml",".claude/skills/wai